# Kinvara semgrepignore (T-133).
#
# THIS FILE IS LOAD-BEARING AND IT IS NOT A COPY OF .gitignore.
#
# Measured on semgrep 1.176.1: with NO .semgrepignore, semgrep applies its own
# built-in defaults, which exclude `test/` and `tests/` directories. A planted
# marker in packages/policy/test/p.test.ts and packages/policy/tests/p.ts was
# NOT scanned, while packages/policy/src/p.ts, src/p.spec.ts and __tests__/p.ts
# were — i.e. a rule that must hold across packages/policy silently did not
# apply to two ordinary directory names, at exit 0.
#
# So this file exists to REPLACE those defaults with an explicit list. Test
# code is scanned deliberately: `any` in a policy test is the same defect as
# `any` in policy source, and SD §DH-2 scopes the rule to packages/policy with
# no test exemption.
#
# Anything added here removes coverage. Add a path only with a reason.

# Dependencies and build output — nothing here is our source.
node_modules/
dist/
build/
out/
.next/
.turbo/
coverage/

# Caches and stores, never source.
.pnpm-store/
.cache/
.git/
